/-!
# Actual coordinate one-cocycles and integer-affine torus chains

This entry point provides integral coordinate cocycles on every product torus,
their literal positive-period normalization, the corresponding actual singular
cohomology classes, and their pullbacks to original period tori.

Integer-affine simplices and all their edges use the genuine quotient topology.
Their formal-chain realization preserves native boundaries and the actual
addition–cross product.  The displayed Alexander–Whitney evaluations are
therefore evaluations on actual singular chains.
-/
